      "name": "MemoryCopyDuffsDevice",
      "signature": "void MemoryCopyDuffsDevice(int nOffsetSrc, int nOffsetDst, int nTableIdx)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Copies memory from multiple source tables to destination using Duff's device optimization. __fastcall: ECX=src offset, EDX=dst offset, Stack[4]=table index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter to 0\n2. For each table iteration:\n   - Load source base from DAT_6faae0dc table\n   - Load destination base from DAT_6faae064 table  \n   - Read operation size from DAT_6faae0a0 table\n   - Copy bytes from (src + offsets[idx]) to (dst + offsets[idx])\n3. Duff's device: switch on size to copy in blocks (1, 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 32 bytes)\n4. Iterate 15 times (increment by 4 until >= 0x3c)\n\nParameters:\n- ECX: nOffsetSrc - Offset into source data\n- EDX: nOffsetDst - Offset into destination data\n- Stack[4]: nTableIdx - Table index selector (IMPLICIT)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3c (60): Total loop iterations (15 * 4)\n- DAT_6faae0dc: Source base address table\n- DAT_6faae064: Destination base address table\n- DAT_6faae0a0: Operation size table\n- 0x6fab1424: Stride increment per iteration",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:93adac5d4956c52f7441201f3f134f8c",
