      "name": "BlendTilePixels",
      "signature": "void BlendTilePixels(int nSrcOffset, int nDstOffset, int nX, int nXDelta, int nY, int nYDelta)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Blend pixels from source tile to destination using lookup table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through 15 blocks (iVar4: 0-14, stride 4)\n2. For each block: fetch size from g_pSizeTable\n3. Calculate destination address using dst base + block address + y-offset\n4. Calculate source address using src base + src offset + x coordinate\n5. Fall-through switch on block size (0x4-0x20, stride 4) to copy bytes\n6. Lookup output color from g_pOutputBuffer using src*256+dst as index\n7. Increment dst offset by stride, x/y coords by deltas\n\nParameters:\n- nSrcOffset: offset into source tile data\n- nDstOffset: destination buffer base offset\n- nX: x-coordinate (subpixel fixed-point)\n- nXDelta: x stride per block\n- nY: y-coordinate (subpixel fixed-point)\n- nYDelta: y stride per block\n\nReturns: void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3c (60): Loop end (15 blocks * 4 bytes)\n- 0x20 (32): Max block size in bytes\n- 0x80: Fixed-point division (>>7 for integer part)\n- 0x100: Lookup table index multiplier",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:cdcb5af10fe229c7047c4417f7d8023b",
