      "name": "DecodeScanlineRLE",
      "signature": "void DecodeScanlineRLE(byte * pbRleData, byte * pbDestBuffer, int nXOffset, int nXStride, int nYOffset, int nYStride, int nScanlineCount, byte byShift)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Decodes and renders RLE-encoded scanline data into output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate base pointer into DAT_6fab51e4 tile table using X/Y offsets and shift\n2. For each scanline:\n   - Read control bytes (run length and pixel count)\n   - If both zero, advance X/Y by stride increments and recalculate tile pointer\n   - Otherwise copy run-length encoded pixels from source\n   - Use switch statement for variable-length run copying (1-32 pixels)\n3. Each pixel fetched from g_pOutputBuffer using source byte + tile palette * 256\n\nParameters:\n- pbRleData (byte*): RLE-encoded scanline data stream\n- pbDestBuffer (byte*): Destination buffer for decoded output\n- nXOffset (int): Starting X coordinate\n- nXStride (int): X increment between scanlines\n- nYOffset (int): Starting Y coordinate\n- nYStride (int): Y increment between scanlines\n- nScanlineCount (int): Number of scanlines to decode\n- byShift (byte): Bit shift amount for coordinate division\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Tile width/height in pixels\n- 0x100 (256): Palette stride multiplier\n- 2: RLE header size (2 bytes per run)\n- Shift amount: Divides coordinates for tile addressing",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f8dcc16a0a4e99eb0fac39eddc9293e1",
