      "name": "DrawSpriteClipped",
      "signature": "void DrawSpriteClipped(byte * pbSrcData, int nXOffset, int nYPos)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Renders sprite data to screen buffer with boundary clipping.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate screen coordinates against clip boundaries (BoundMask2, MaxY, ClipY, ScreenDim)\n2. For clipped region: Copy pixel data using optimized word/byte copies with RLE skip handling\n3. For unclipped region: Iterate through row RLE commands, apply row-level clipping, copy valid pixels\n4. Handle pixel overflow via clipping window calculations\n\nParameters:\n- pbSrcData (byte*): Sprite RLE-encoded data (skip bytes, then pixel data pairs)\n- nXOffset (int): Horizontal pixel offset in screen buffer\n- nYPos (int): Vertical row position for rendering\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Row iteration count for clipped paths\n- 0xffffffff: Invalid row marker for assertion check\n- g_dwStrideIncrement: Bytes between screen rows\n- g_dwMaxPixelValue, g_dwClipWindowHeight: Clipping boundary calculations",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:052a101a230c3ddc22bbf8ff66201a19",
