      "name": "DrawPixelRow",
      "signature": "void DrawPixelRow(byte * pbSrcPixels, int nX, int nY, uint dwPaletteIdx)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Draws a row of pixels to the screen buffer using palette lookup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate X coordinate is within left/right clip bounds\n2. Validate Y coordinate is within top/bottom screen bounds\n3. Look up row offset from g_aRowOffsetTable using Y coordinate\n4. Calculate destination buffer position combining row offset and X coordinate\n5. Extract palette index from low 8 bits and shift right by 3 bits\n6. If initialization counter is 0, assert buffer and reinitialize palette\n7. Check if region fits within inner clip bounds for fast path\n8. If within bounds, call CopyDataWithLookup for aligned region copy\n9. Otherwise call DrawRowPixelsWithPalette for pixel-by-pixel rendering with clipping\n\nParameters:\n  pbSrcPixels: Source pixel data buffer to render\n  nX: X coordinate (column) on screen (validated against screen width)\n  nY: Y coordinate (row) on screen (validated against screen height)\n  dwPaletteIdx: Palette index encoded in bits, extracted and shifted for lookup\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If initialization counter is 0, triggers buffer validation and reinitialization\n  - Inner clip region uses fast CopyDataWithLookup for performance\n  - Outer region uses slower DrawRowPixelsWithPalette with per-pixel clipping",
