      "name": "RenderRLESpriteWithAlphaBlend",
      "signature": "void RenderRLESpriteWithAlphaBlend(byte * pbRleData, int nPosX, int nPosY, byte byAlphaLevel)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Renders an RLE-compressed sprite with alpha blending to the screen buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Select palette lookup table based on alpha level threshold:\n   - byAlphaLevel >= 0xC0: Use g_pSourceData[0] (75% opacity)\n   - byAlphaLevel >= 0x80: Use g_pSourceData[1] (50% opacity)\n   - byAlphaLevel >= 0x40: Use g_pSourceData[2] (25% opacity)\n   - byAlphaLevel < 0x40: Early return (fully transparent)\n2. Validate Y position against screen bounds (g_dwBoundMask2 to g_dwMaxY)\n3. Validate X position against screen bounds (g_dwClipY to g_dwScreenDim)\n4. Assert g_dwInitializationCounter is non-zero (screen buffer initialized)\n5. Calculate destination pointer: g_aRowOffsetTable[nPosY] + g_dwInitializationCounter + nPosX\n6. If fully within inner clip region (fast path):\n   - Process 32 rows without bounds checking\n   - Read RLE pair (skip_count, run_length) per row\n   - If both zero: advance to next row (add g_dwStrideIncrement)\n   - Otherwise: skip pixels, then blend run_length pixels\n7. Else use clipped path with per-pixel bounds checking:\n   - Track current row index and check against g_dwMaxYPos\n   - Calculate clip offsets for left/right clipping\n   - Skip pixels outside clip region\n   - Blend visible pixels using same palette lookup formula\n\nParameters:\n  pbRleData (ECX) - Pointer to RLE-compressed sprite data\n  nPosX (EDX) - X coordinate for rendering position\n  nPosY (stack+0x4) - Y coordinate for rendering position\n  byAlphaLevel (stack+0x8) - Alpha transparency level (0x40=25%, 0x80=50%, 0xC0=75%)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nRLE Format:\n  Each row encoded as pairs: [skip_count][run_length][pixel_data...]\n  skip_count=0 and run_length=0 indicates end of row\n\nAlpha Blending:\n  Uses precomputed palette lookup: dest = palette[src_pixel + dest_pixel * 256]\n  Three palette tables indexed by alpha level provide different transparency\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early return if byAlphaLevel < 0x40 (fully transparent)\n  - Early return if position outside screen bounds\n  - Assertion failure and exit if screen buffer not initialized\n  - Early return if clipped row exceeds g_dwMaxYPos",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:052a101a230c3ddc22bbf8ff66201a19",
