      "name": "RenderImageRowPixels",
      "signature": "void RenderImageRowPixels(int nImage, int nXOffset, int nClipX, int nDestBuffer, dword nPaletteIdx)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Renders image row pixels with optional palette translation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check image flag (param_1+0x8 & 4) to select rendering path\n2. If flag not set: direct pixel copy loop with source/dest table lookups\n   - Calculate horizontal clip boundary and max row count (0xf)\n   - Iterate through rows, applying source/destination base offsets\n   - Copy bytes from source to destination using palette color lookup\n3. If flag set: call DrawRowPixelsWithPalette for alternative rendering\n\nParameters:\n- nImage: Image structure pointer (flags at +0x8, data at +0x10)\n- nXOffset: Horizontal pixel offset in destination\n- nClipX: Horizontal clipping value\n- nDestBuffer: Destination buffer pointer\n- nPaletteIdx: Palette index (bits 3-7 select palette table offset)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x4: Image flag mask (bit 2 = use alternate renderer)\n- 0xf (15): Maximum row iteration count\n- 0x40 (64): Palette table stride\n- 0x10: Offset to image data pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
