      "name": "ProcessTileRenderList",
      "signature": "void ProcessTileRenderList(void * pRenderList, int nBaseX, int nYOffset, void * pBlendParams)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes a render list of tile elements and dispatches to rendering functions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate base destination offset from stride and Y offset\n2. Exit early if render list count is zero (pRenderList+0x50)\n3. For each element in render list (stride 0x14 bytes):\n   a. Get element pointer from list base (pRenderList+0x54)\n   b. Calculate destination buffer from element X/Y offsets\n   c. Skip if element flag bit 0 not set (element disabled)\n4. Validate screen coordinates against clipping bounds:\n   - g_dwBoundMask1 <= dwScreenX < g_dwMaxYCoord\n   - g_dwClipMinY <= dwYOffset < g_dwScreenWidth\n5. Select rendering mode based on g_fSimpleRenderMode:\n   - Simple mode: Use palette index directly from blend params\n   - Complex mode: Calculate blend parameters from 4-corner values\n6. Calculate color variance (sum of absolute differences)\n   - If variance <= 9 or g_dwFlagState set: use simple palette\n   - Otherwise: compute averaged blend coordinates\n7. Check inner clip region for fast path:\n   - g_dwOffset1 <= dwScreenX < g_dwMaxYPos2\n   - g_dwAdjustedWidth <= dwYOffset < g_dwClipMinX\n8. Dispatch to appropriate renderer based on flags:\n   - Outside clip + simple: RenderImageRowPixels\n   - Outside clip + complex: RenderTileLineNormal\n   - Inside clip + simple + no RLE: MemoryCopyDuffsDevice\n   - Inside clip + simple + RLE: CopyDataWithLookup\n   - Inside clip + complex + no RLE: BlendTilePixels\n   - Inside clip + complex + RLE: DecodeScanlineRLE\n9. Advance to next element (offset += 0x14)\n\nParameters:\n- pRenderList: Pointer to render list structure\n  +0x50: Element count (int)\n  +0x54: Pointer to element array\n- nBaseX: Base X coordinate for rendering\n- nYOffset: Y offset for screen position\n- pBlendParams: Blend parameter table for color interpolation\n\nReturns: void\n\nElement Structure (0x14 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field         Description\n0x00    2     nXOffset      X offset from base\n0x02    2     nYPos         Y position\n0x06    1     byBlendType   Blend type index low\n0x07    1     byBlendShift  Blend type index high (multiplied by 8)\n0x08    1     byFlags       Render flags (bit 0=enabled, bit 2=RLE)\n0x10    4     pSrcData      Pointer to source image data\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x14: Element stride in render list\n- 0x0c: Blend param record size\n- 0x40: Palette table stride\n- 0xf (15): Max row count for rendering\n- 0x7: RLE decode shift\n- 9: Color variance threshold for simple vs complex blend\n\nFlag Bits (byFlags at +0x08):\n- 0x01: Element enabled\n- 0x04: RLE encoded data",
