      "name": "GfxIsVideoDisabled",
      "signature": "bool GfxIsVideoDisabled(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Checks if video output is disabled (graphics interface uninitialized or video param is zero).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_pGfxInterface pointer from global at 0x6fabd21c\n2. Test if interface pointer is NULL\n3. If NULL, return false (graphics not initialized)\n4. Load g_dwVideoParam from global at 0x6fabd22c\n5. Test if video parameter equals zero\n6. Return true if param==0 (video disabled), false otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- bool: true if graphics interface is valid AND video parameter is zero (disabled state)\n        false if graphics interface is NULL OR video parameter is non-zero (enabled)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns false for uninitialized graphics (NULL interface pointer)\n- Intended semantic: \"Is video currently disabled?\" where 0 = disabled, non-zero = enabled\n\nCross-References:\n- g_pGfxInterface (0x6fabd21c): Graphics interface vtable pointer, set by InitializeGraphicsSystem\n- g_dwVideoParam (0x6fabd22c): Video parameter flag, set by InitializeGraphicsSystem/SetVideoParameter",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
