      "name": "IsStateLevelFourOrHigher",
      "signature": "bool IsStateLevelFourOrHigher(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Checks if the global state level has reached level 4 or higher.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the current global state level value from g_dwStateLevel\n2. Compare the state level against threshold value 4\n3. Return true if state level >= 4, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\ntrue  - State level is 4 or higher (advanced game state)\nfalse - State level is 3 or lower (early game state)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 4 (0x4) represents the threshold between early and advanced game states.\nThe comparison uses signed integer arithmetic with SETGE instruction.",
