      "comment": "GfxInterface_CallMethod0x4C - Graphics Interface Vtable Dispatch Thunk\n\nCLASSIFICATION: Thunk/Wrapper - Dispatches to graphics interface vtable method at offset 0x4C\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_pGfxInterface pointer from global storage (0x6fabd21c)\n2. Tail-call JMP to vtable method at offset 0x4C (no stack frame created)\n\nParameters:\nNone - this is a zero-parameter thunk\n\nReturns:\nPass-through - return value depends on vtable method at offset 0x4C\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- g_pGfxInterface must be initialized (set by InitializeGraphicsSystem) before calling\n- Uses tail-call optimization via JMP - no local stack frame, return goes directly to original caller\n- Offset 0x4C likely corresponds to a rendering or display update operation\n\nVtable Reference (g_pGfxInterface offsets):\n0x28 - Ordinal_10046\n0x4C - THIS METHOD\n0x5C - GfxInterface_CallMethod0x5C (Ordinal_10019)\n0x84 - GfxInterfaceCall84\n0xA0 - GfxInterface_DrawRectangle\n0xA8 - Ordinal_10051\n0xC4 - GfxInterface_CallMethod0xC4\n\nCross-References:\n- Entry Point\n- Address 0x6faad0ec\n- Uses: g_pGfxInterface (0x6fabd21c)",
