      "signature": "void GfxInterface_CallMethod0xAC(uint dwParam1, byte byParam2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Stdcall-to-fastcall thunk for graphics interface vtable method at offset 0xAC.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - translates calling convention for internal graphics dispatch.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_pGfxInterface global pointer into EAX\n2. Move byParam2 (byte from stack+8) into DL register\n3. Move dwParam1 (dword from stack+4) into ECX register\n4. Call indirect through vtable at [EAX + 0xAC]\n5. Return with 8-byte stack cleanup (__stdcall)\n\nParameters:\n- dwParam1 (uint): First parameter forwarded to graphics method via ECX\n- byParam2 (byte): Second parameter forwarded to graphics method via DL\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nDecompiler Discrepancy:\nThe decompiler shows parameters as unused because it doesn't recognize the\nstdcall-to-fastcall calling convention translation. Assembly confirms both\nparameters are loaded and passed via registers to the indirect call.\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GfxInterface_CallMethod0xA8 (0x6faa3cd0): Same pattern, offset 0xA8\n- GfxInterface_CallMethod0xB0 (0x6faa3d10): Same pattern, offset 0xB0\n- g_pGfxInterface (0x6fabd21c): Global graphics interface pointer",
