      "name": "FOG_SetGameFlagsAndDraw",
      "signature": "void FOG_SetGameFlagsAndDraw(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets game flags to FOG_FLAG_DRAW (0x100) and invokes the graphics draw handler.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - sets flags then tail calls to graphics draw routine\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load graphics interface vtable pointer from g_pGfxInterface (0x6fabd21c)\n2. Set g_dwGameFlags (0x6faae490) to 0x100 (FOG_FLAG_DRAW)\n3. Tail jump to draw handler at vtable offset 0x54\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: g_pGfxInterface - Graphics interface vtable pointer at 0x6fabd21c\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwGameFlags - Receives 0x100 flag value at 0x6faae490\n\nReturns:\n- void (tail call to draw handler, return handled by callee)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x100: FOG_FLAG_DRAW - Indicates draw operation in progress\n- 0x54: Offset of Draw method in graphics interface vtable\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FOG_GetGameFlags: Returns g_dwGameFlags value\n- GfxDrawAndUpdateFrameIndex: Similar but stores frame index instead of flags\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function uses tail call optimization (JMP instead of CALL+RET)\n- Unlike GfxDrawAndUpdateFrameIndex which stores frame index, this sets specific flag value\n- Exported ordinal interface for Fog.dll",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:6fafd9d61e995ac46683353d63a5b0e1",
