      "name": "ClampFrameIndexToUpperBound",
      "signature": "void ClampFrameIndexToUpperBound(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Clamps frame index back toward upper bound when it exceeds limit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_dwCurrentFrameIndex into EAX\n2. If index <= 0x100 (256), exit unchanged\n3. Subtract 0x20 (32) from index\n4. Store adjusted value to g_dwCurrentFrameIndex\n5. If adjusted value >= 0x100, exit (still valid)\n6. If adjusted value < 0x100, clamp UP to 0x100\n\nParameters:\n- None (operates on global state)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n- g_dwCurrentFrameIndex (0x6faae48c): Adjusted toward 0x100 bound\n\nCallers:\n- Export table (Ordinal 10063)\n- Referenced from 0x6faad194\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GfxDrawAndUpdateFrameIndex: Reads g_dwCurrentFrameIndex\n- IncrementFrameIndex: Reads/writes g_dwCurrentFrameIndex\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x100 (256): Upper bound / target clamp value\n- 0x20 (32): Decrement step per call\n\nDecompiler Discrepancy:\nThe decompiler shows inverted conditional logic. Assembly shows:\n- JLE at 0x6faa3faa exits if EAX <= 0x100 (no adjustment needed)\n- JGE at 0x6faa3fb9 exits if adjusted >= 0x100 (valid after subtract)\n- Final MOV clamps UP to 0x100 when subtraction overshoots below bound",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
