      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Wrapper that calls the graphics interface rendering function with specified parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load parameter 7 (dwParam7) from stack\n2. Load parameter 6 (dwParam6) from stack\n3. Load parameter 5 (dwParam5) from stack\n4. Push params 5-7 and params 3-4 onto stack\n5. Load graphics interface pointer from global g_pGfxInterface\n6. Call function at offset 0x80 in graphics interface structure\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- dwUnused1: Loaded from stack but not used in function call\n- dwUnused2: Loaded from stack but not used in function call\n- dwParam3: Third parameter passed to graphics interface function\n- dwParam4: Fourth parameter passed to graphics interface function\n- dwParam5: Fifth parameter passed to graphics interface function\n- dwParam6: Sixth parameter passed to graphics interface function\n- dwParam7: Seventh parameter passed to graphics interface function\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nNotes:\n- This is a thin wrapper over a graphics interface virtual function\n- Parameters 1-2 appear to be unused (likely compiler artifacts or placeholders)\n- The actual graphics operation is determined by the function pointer at g_pGfxInterface[0x80]",
