      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Wrapper that invokes function pointer at offset 0x84 in graphics interface structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load parameters 3-6 into registers (EDX, ECX, EAX, stack)\n2. Call function pointer at g_pGfxInterface[0x84]\n3. Return to caller (stdcall: caller cleans 0x18 bytes from stack)\n\nParameters:\n- dwUnused1, dwUnused2: Not used by this function\n- dwParam3 (uint): Passed as 3rd argument to interface function\n- dwParam4 (uint): Passed as 4th argument to interface function\n- dwParam5 (uint): Passed as 1st argument to interface function (EDX)\n- dwParam6 (uint): Passed as 2nd argument to interface function (EAX)\n\nReturns:\n- void (direct pass-through of interface call result via EAX)",
