      "name": "InitializeGfxInterface",
      "signature": "uint InitializeGfxInterface(uint dwRendererMode, uint dwResolutionMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Initializes the graphics interface, creates the main window, and configures display settings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if main window already exists via FindWindowA\n2. If window exists, show critical error (duplicate instance)\n3. If not, validate graphics interface and initial flags\n4. Store rendering mode and resolution mode to globals\n5. Calculate window dimensions based on resolution mode (640x480/800x600/1280x1024)\n6. Calculate window style flags based on rendering mode (windowed vs fullscreen)\n7. Adjust window rect for borders/title bar using AdjustWindowRectEx\n8. Calculate centering position on desktop if windowed mode\n9. If system screen too small (&lt;800x600), apply display settings change to 800x600\n10. Create main window with calculated parameters\n11. Initialize graphics library through graphics interface function pointers\n12. Return success/failure status in EAX\n\nParameters:\n- dwRendererMode (EAX/Stack[0x4]): Rendering mode (1=windowed, other=fullscreen)\n- dwResolutionMode (EDX/Stack[0x8]): Resolution (0=640x480, 1-2=800x600, 3=1280x1024, other=error)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success (window created and graphics initialized)\n- 0 on failure (window creation failed or graphics init failed)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x280 (640): Standard game width for 640x480 mode\n- 0x1e0 (480): Standard game height for 640x480 mode\n- 0x320 (800): Standard width for other modes\n- 0x258 (600): Standard height for 800x600 mode\n- 0x540 (1280): Width for high-res mode\n- 0x2bc (700): Height for 1280x1024 mode\n- 0xc00000: Window style flag for windowed mode (WS_OVERLAPPEDWINDOW)\n- 0x80080000: Fullscreen style flags\n- 0x86080000: Fullscreen style flags with specific settings\n- 0x40000: Extended window style (WS_EX_CLIENTEDGE)\n- 0x40008: CreateWindowEx extended styles\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FindWindowA (check existing window)\n- CreateWindowExA (create main window)\n- AdjustWindowRectEx (calculate window size)\n- ChangeDisplaySettingsA (apply display mode)\n- GetSystemMetrics (get desktop dimensions)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
