      "name": "ShowOrHideCursor",
      "signature": "void ShowOrHideCursor(int nShowCursor)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Controls cursor visibility based on video mode and parameter flag.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwVideoParam is initialized and video mode is standard (not 4-6)\n2. If nShowCursor == 0: If display not initialized, show cursor (ShowCursor 1) until count < 0, set flag\n3. If nShowCursor != 0: If display initialized, hide cursor (ShowCursor 0) until count >= 0, clear flag\n4. Video modes 4-6 skip all cursor operations\n\nParameters:\n- nShowCursor (int): Control flag (0=show cursor, non-0=hide cursor)\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwVideoParam (global display enabled flag)\n- IMPLICIT: g_nVideoMode (current video mode)\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwDisplayInitialized (display state flag)\n- IMPLICIT: g_pShowCursor (function pointer at 0x6faac160)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nRelated Globals:\n- 0x6fabd22c: g_dwVideoParam (video initialization flag)\n- 0x6fabd228: g_nVideoMode (current video mode, skip if 4-6)\n- 0x6faae5c8: g_dwDisplayInitialized (cursor display state)\n- 0x6faac160: g_pShowCursor (ShowCursor API function pointer)",
