      "name": "HideAppBarWindows",
      "signature": "void HideAppBarWindows(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Hide AppBar windows (taskbar equivalents) on specified edges.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if video parameter is set (g_dwVideoParam == 1 means fullscreen, skip hiding)\n2. Initialize AppBar structure with size 0x24 and window handle from g_dwInitFlag\n3. Loop through 4 edges (0-3: ABE_LEFT, ABE_TOP, ABE_RIGHT, ABE_BOTTOM)\n4. For each edge, call SHAppBarMessage(ABM_GETAUTOHIDEBAR) to find AppBar window\n5. If AppBar window exists, save window placement and hide it with ShowWindow(SW_HIDE)\n6. Store window handle in global array g_pAppBars for later restoration\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwVideoParam - video mode flag (1=fullscreen)\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwInitFlag - window handle to use as AppBar owner\n- IMPLICIT: g_pAppBars - array to store 4 hidden window handles\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24 (36): APPBARDATA structure size\n- 0x2c (44): WINDOWPLACEMENT structure size\n- 0xc (12): Stride for 3x UINT_PTR in window array\n- 0x6fabd708: End boundary of AppBar window array",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:031581a1b0085e45e2935ed859088232",
