      "name": "ExecuteUnitActionWithSEH",
      "signature": "int ExecuteUnitActionWithSEH(void * pUnitOrState, dword dwParam2, dword dwParam3, dword dwParam4, dword dwParam5, dword dwParam6, dword dwParam7)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Executes a unit action handler within Structured Exception Handling (SEH) frame.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up SEH exception frame for Windows-level exception handling\n2. Initialize exception context variables on stack (handler offset, exception list)\n3. Store caller parameters and handler function pointer in local variables\n4. Dereference param_1 to get unit data value (uVar2 = *pUnitOrState)\n5. Call FUN_6fb9c171() to retrieve action handler structure (pDVar1)\n6. Execute handler callback via function pointer at offset 0x68 in handler structure\n7. On exception jump to 0x6fb99ed3: Restore exception list from FS:[0], restore exception links\n8. On normal path (no exception): Restore FS:[0] to previous exception handler, return 0\n\nParameters:\n- pUnitOrState: Pointer to unit/game object or state structure (dereferenced at [pUnitOrState])\n- dwParam2-dwParam7: Caller-provided parameters passed to the action handler\n\nReturns:\n- int: Always returns 0 on successful completion\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Windows SEH exceptions trigger jump to 0x6fb99ed3 (exception recovery path)\n- pExceptionStackPtr/pExceptionBasePtr capture stack frame pointers for exception tracking\n- ExceptionList global links all exception handlers in thread\n- Compiler SSA variables: uVar2 (dereferenced unit value), pDVar1 (handler structure), ppvVar3 (pointer to unit parameter)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x68: Offset to callback function pointer in handler structure\n- 0x6fb99f01: Exception handler entry point address\n- 0x6fb99ed3: Exception recovery code address\n- 0x34: Total stack frame size (SUB ESP, 0x34)\n\nStructure Layout (SEH Frame):\n| Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-----------|------|-------------|\n| 0x34   | 4    | nException| int  | Exception result flag |\n| 0x30   | 4    | pUnit     | void*| Unit pointer copy |\n| 0x2c   | 4    | pParam3Copy| void*| Param3 copy |\n| 0x28   | 4    | pfnHandler| void*| Handler function |\n| 0x24   | 4    | dwParam5  | dword| Param5 copy |\n| 0x20   | 4    | dwParam2  | dword| Param2 copy |\n| 0x1c   | 4    | dwParam6  | dword| Param6 copy |\n| 0x18   | 4    | dwParam7  | dword| Param7 copy |\n| 0x14   | 4    | dwHandler | dword| Exception handler offset (0x6fb99ed3) |\n| 0x10   | 4    | Reserved  | dword| Cleared for exception state |\n| -      | 4x4  | ExceptionFrame | dword[]| Windows SEH frame structure |",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
