      "name": "InitializeSEHHandler",
      "signature": "void InitializeSEHHandler(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize structured exception handling (SEH) frame for the current function scope.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push -0x1 (exception handler scope marker indicating function-level handler)\n2. Save current EAX register to stack\n3. Load current exception handler chain head from FS:[0x0]\n4. Push saved handler pointer (chain linkage)\n5. Write new exception handler base address to FS:[0x0] pointing to ESP\n6. Save return address parameter at [ESP+0xc]\n7. Initialize EBP frame pointer at [ESP+0xc] offset\n8. Push saved EAX to create 12-byte SEH frame structure\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Called via PUSH EAX, RET pair - exception handler parameter passed in EAX on exception\n- FS:[0x0] points to SEH frame structure on stack\n- Stack frame must be exactly 12 bytes (3 DWORDs) for handler chain compatibility\n- Note: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary (auStack_c) optimized away by compiler\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xFFFFFFFF (-0x1) - SEH scope marker for function-level exception handler\n0x0 - FS segment offset for exception handler chain pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:5eebfcd0189b5203a29c76a57896a0fd",
