      "name": "CppExceptionFilterForUnitActions",
      "signature": "int CppExceptionFilterForUnitActions(PEXCEPTION_RECORD pExceptionRecord, PVOID pContext, DWORD dwErrorCode, dword dwDispatcherContext, dword nActionId, int nExceptionOffset, int nRangeIndex, PVOID pDispatcher)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "C++ exception filter for unit action execution with range validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current state data via FUN_6fb9c171()\n2. Check if special flag 0x1a is set; if so, execute unit action with SEH\n3. If action succeeds (nResult != 0), return early\n4. Call SearchRangeTable to get range entry array and bounds (nStartIndex, nEndIndex)\n5. Iterate through range entries from nStartIndex to nEndIndex\n6. For each entry, check if nRangeIndex falls within [min, max] bounds\n7. Calculate entry offset: (field[12] << 4) + field[16]\n8. Load pointer at offset-12; if NULL or char[8] is null terminator, proceed\n9. Call FUN_6fb9bc8d to process matching range entry\n10. Continue to next entry and repeat\n\nParameters:\n- PEXCEPTION_RECORD pExceptionRecord: Exception information record\n- PVOID pContext: Context data pointer\n- DWORD dwErrorCode: Error code from exception\n- dword dwDispatcherContext: Dispatcher state (0x00-0xFF, check against range bounds)\n- dword nActionId: Action identifier for validation\n- int nRangeIndex: Range index to search within table\n- int nActionLevel: Action level/priority value\n- PVOID pUserData: User-supplied context pointer\n\nReturns:\n- int: 0 if range processing succeeded, 1 if action executed via SEH early exit\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic offset 0x68: State data flag check\n- Magic offset 12 and 16: Range entry indices (5-dword entries)\n- Magic offset -12 and -16: Pointer and header offsets within entry\n- Magic offset 8: Character check for null terminator\n\nRange Table Entry Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n  0      | 4    | min        | int  | Minimum range value\n  4      | 4    | max        | int  | Maximum range value\n  8      | 4    | reserved   | int  | Unused\n  12     | 4    | field1     | int  | Multiplier for offset calculation (<<4)\n  16     | 4    | field2     | int  | Base offset addend",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:2436a61b7e4d275a18f76f4f3176d3e0",
