      "name": "MatchItemSlotsByIdentityAndFlags",
      "signature": "dword MatchItemSlotsByIdentityAndFlags(byte * pItemSlot1, byte * pItemSlot2, dword * pdwFlagMask)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Match item slots by identity and apply flag filters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load item name pointer from pItemSlot1[+4]; if NULL or points to empty string, return SUCCESS (1)\n2. Compare item pointers: if pItemSlot1[+4] == pItemSlot2[+4], skip string comparison\n3. If different pointers, compare item name strings: strcmp(pItemSlot1[+4]+8, pItemSlot2[+4]+8)\n4. If string comparison succeeds (iVar1==0), proceed to flag checks\n5. Flag filter validation (all must pass):\n   - If FLAG_0x02 set in pdwFlagMask: require FLAG_0x08 SET in pItemSlot1, else FAIL (return 0)\n   - If FLAG_0x01 set in pdwFlagMask: require FLAG_0x01 SET in pItemSlot1, else FAIL\n   - If FLAG_0x02 set in pdwFlagMask: require FLAG_0x02 SET in pItemSlot1, else FAIL\n6. If all flags pass, return SUCCESS (1); else return FAIL (0)\n\nParameters:\npItemSlot1 (byte *) - First item slot pointer with flags at offset 0, item name pointer at offset +4\npItemSlot2 (byte *) - Second item slot pointer with flags at offset 0, item name pointer at offset +4\npdwFlagMask (dword *) - Points to dword with filter flags (0x01, 0x02) indicating which flags to check\n\nReturns:\n1 - Items match by identity/name and all enabled flag filters pass\n0 - Items do not match or flag filter fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL or empty item names (at pItemSlot1[+4]+8) immediately return SUCCESS (1)\n- Flag mask 0 (no filters) means all items match once identity passes\n- Asymmetric flag checking: filters from pItemSlot1, mask from pdwFlagMask",
