      "name": "ExecuteSehFilterAndHandler",
      "signature": "uint ExecuteSehFilterAndHandler(void * pExceptionRecord, void * pEstablisherFrame, void * pContext, void * pDispatcherContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Walks SEH scope table entries executing filter and handler functions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check exception flags - if unwinding (flags & 6), call __local_unwind2 and return\n2. Store exception context in stack locals for filter access\n3. Iterate through scope table (12-byte entries) from current scope\n4. For each scope with a filter, call filter function\n5. If filter returns negative, return 0 (continue search)\n6. If filter returns positive, perform global/local unwind and call handler\n7. Continue to next scope entry (linked list via first field)\n\nParameters:\n- pExceptionRecord: EXCEPTION_RECORD pointer passed in ECX\n- pEstablisherFrame: Stack frame pointer passed in EDX\n- pContext: CONTEXT record pointer\n- pDispatcherContext: DISPATCHER_CONTEXT pointer\n- pFunctionEntry: RUNTIME_FUNCTION entry pointer\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Exception not handled (filter returned negative)\n- 1: Exception handled or unwinding complete\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6: EH_UNWINDING | EH_EXIT_UNWIND flags\n- 0xC (12): Scope table entry stride\n- -1: End of scope chain sentinel",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:e875dee7a1e28a3519eff4a0307e3874",
