      "name": "ValidateStreamPropertyId",
      "signature": "void ValidateStreamPropertyId(uint dwOsError)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Maps a Windows OS error code to a C runtime errno value.\n\nCalled from stream I/O functions (SeekStream, FileWriteData) to translate\nWindows error codes to POSIX-compatible errno values after failed operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6faaad04 to get OS error storage pointer and store dwOsError\n2. Search g_adwOsErrorToErrnoTable (45 entries, 8-byte stride) for matching OS error\n   - Entry format: [uint dwOsError, uint dwErrno]\n   - Table spans 0x6fab0f70 to 0x6fab10d8 (360 bytes)\n3. If match found: set errno to corresponding table value at [index*8 + 0x6fab0f74]\n4. If no match, apply range-based fallbacks:\n   - Range 0x13-0x24: Set errno = 0x0D (EACCES - permission denied)\n   - Range 0xBC-0xCA: Set errno = 0x08 (ENOEXEC - exec format error)\n   - Default: Set errno = 0x16 (EINVAL - invalid argument)\n\nParameters:\n  dwOsError - Windows error code from GetLastError or similar\n\nReturns:\n  void - Sets errno via GetErrnoPointer()\n\nTable Structure (g_adwOsErrorToErrnoTable):\n  Offset  Size  Field        Type  Description\n  0x0     4     dwOsError    uint  Windows error code\n  0x4     4     dwErrno      uint  Corresponding errno value\n\nError Ranges:\n  0x13-0x24 (19-36):  EACCES (0x0D/13) - Access denied / sharing violation range\n  0xBC-0xCA (188-202): ENOEXEC (0x08/8) - Executable format errors\n  Default:            EINVAL (0x16/22) - Invalid argument",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:ef14b972a786ba8645bf0ac0ecb3d27f",
