      "comment": "Removes a node from its current doubly-linked list and inserts it into a target list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pListBase parameter (EBX implicit) to determine source node list base\n2. Calculate source node address: if pListBase==0 then pBase+1, else *(pBase)+pListBase\n3. Load first source node pointer and test if node is linked (non-zero)\n4. If source node exists in list:\n   a. Load backpointer value from source node[1]\n   b. Test backpointer sign bit (bit 31): if negative, treat as direct pointer via NOT\n   c. If positive, calculate actual backpointer by subtracting node[1] offset from source address\n   d. Unlink source node by updating backpointer target to point to source node's next\n   e. Update source node's next link to point to source node's previous\n   f. Zero out source node's next and previous pointers\n5. Validate nLinkMode parameter to determine target list base\n6. Calculate target list address: if nLinkMode==0 then pBase+1, else *(pBase)+nLinkMode\n7. Test nSecondOffset mode (DEC to test for value 1):\n   a. If nSecondOffset != 1 (copy mode):\n      - Load node at target address\n      - Copy that node to source node position\n      - Copy backpointer from copied node\n      - Update copied node's backpointer to reference pListBase (restore original location)\n      - Link source node into target list\n   b. If nSecondOffset == 1 (insert mode):\n      - Copy target node pointer into source position\n      - Copy target node's backpointer\n      - Test backpointer sign bit\n      - If negative: update backpointer via direct NOT address\n      - If positive: calculate actual address using base adjustment if needed, then update backpointer\n      - Update target node's backpointer to reference pListBase\n\nParameters:\n- pListBase (EBX implicit): Base structure pointer containing list header offsets\n- nSecondOffset (stack): Mode flag (1=insert, other=copy/swap existing node)\n- nLinkMode (stack): Offset to target list header from base structure\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies linked lists in-place via pointer manipulation)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Negative offsets (bit 31 set) are treated as direct pointers after bitwise NOT operation\n- Zero offset (0x0) uses direct addressing at pBase+1 offset\n- Function handles both singly-linked (backpointer 0) and doubly-linked structures\n- Backpointer field can store either negative direct address or positive offset pair\n- Base parameter can be negative, triggering address adjustment via node header field",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
